# netsurf: structural flips on youtube's iframes answered locally -- quoted attributes bounded, leaf boxes restyled in place (patch 406)
# Generated 2026-11-08
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 405)
#
# After 405, youtube's 7 structural full rebuilds remained. A debug build
# (scratch only) logged them: 6 not narrow because an UNBOUNDED compound
# matched -- .vEFDtd:last-child[data-expand-type="1"] and its twin,
# unbounded only for the quotes in their attribute value; the 7th narrow,
# but the sibling to restyle an <iframe> (a bare :last-child-type compound
# on the previous one), whose box is never rebuilt (patch 371).
#
#  - html_rl_struct_parse_cp: a quoted value inside [...] no longer
#    unbounds the compound (attributes are ignored: a broader match); the
#    [...] skip honours quotes. A quote outside [...], a backslash anywhere
#    or a '|' outside [...] (a namespace) still unbounds.
#  - html_rl_leaf_restyle: a matching child whose box has no children (an
#    <iframe>, an <img>; in a line too) gets a new computed style on the
#    same box (as html_reconvert_fast_style), from its CSS parent (the
#    block whose children changed), and the page is laid out whole.
#    Nothing freed: the frame's box and window stay. Declined into the full
#    rebuild when display/float/position change, when a ::before/::after
#    box would be generated (html_rl_pseudo_generates mirrors
#    box_construct_generate: never for a replaced element, else content
#    not normal and display not none), when either style counts, for a
#    control or a clone.
# Logged "..., leaf boxes in place" on the 405 line; "leaf restyle
# declined (why)".
#
